#
# Component:       contracts
# Module:          contracts/events/topics.psv
# Owning Team:     Platform Enablement Guild (PEG)
# Classification:  INTERNAL
# Purpose:         Registry of every Redpanda topic of AaaS (CLAUDE.md 4.2):
#                  one pipe-separated row per topic. Read by
#                  infra/redpanda/create-topics.sh, which creates the topics,
#                  and by scripts/docs-portal.py (event catalog).
# Related Docs:    CLAUDE.md (section 4.2), ADR-0011, infra/redpanda/README.md,
#                  contracts/events/README.md
#
# Columns: topic|partitions|producer|consumers|purpose
#   topic:      aaas.<entity>.<past-tense-verb>.v<N>; a breaking change is a
#               new row with .v<N+1>, never an edit of an existing name.
#   partitions: number of partitions (messages are keyed by taskId); it may
#               only grow, because Redpanda cannot remove partitions.
#   producer:   the one service that publishes, or `every consumer`.
#   consumers:  comma-separated services, or `(audit)` when no service
#               consumes the topic yet.
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
aaas.key.pressed.v1|3|expression-assembler|(audit)|Every key press of a calculator session.
aaas.expression.submitted.v1|3|expression-assembler|parser, stopwatch|An expression completed by "=" and accepted as a new task.
aaas.addition.requested.v1|3|parser|saga-orchestrator (from P3.3), ledger (until P3.4)|A parsed addition of a and b; from P2.17 validated, with b the smaller operand.
aaas.successor.called.v1|3|successor|(audit)|One computation of n + 1 by the successor service.
aaas.carry.propagated.v1|3|carry|(audit)|One carry propagated to a higher digit position.
aaas.result.voted.v1|3|outbox-relay|ledger|The sum computed by Peano and confirmed by the consensus vote.
aaas.ledger.appended.v1|3|ledger|stopwatch, billing|A result appended to the hash-chained ledger.
aaas.invoice.issued.v1|3|billing|(audit)|A 0.00 PLN invoice issued for a recorded addition.
aaas.dlq.v1|3|every consumer|dead-letter|An event whose processing failed after local retries.
